 |Pityriasis alba |C |Epidermal hyperplasia preferentially involving the | | | | |stratum spinosum | |4 |Pustule |D |Occurs predominantly in | | | | |infants, children and adolescents | |5 |Molluscum contagiosum |E |Elevated solid area more than 5 mm in diameter | |6 |Infantile Eczema |F |Staphylococcus aureus. | |7 |Pemphigus |G |Discrete, pus-filled raised area | |8 |Impetigo |H |Loss of intercellular connections resulting in lack of | | | | |cohesion between keratinocytes | |9 |Condyloma Acunimatum |I |Non-infectious inflammation of the skin | |10 |Superficial fungal infection |J |Human papillomavirus | |11 |Acanthosis |K |Poxvirus | |12 |Nodule |L |Venereal wart | |13 |Acantholysis |M |Blistering disorder caused by autoantibodies | |14 |Papillomatosis |N |Hyperplasia of the papillary dermis with elongation | | | | |and/or widening of the dermal papillae | |15 |Plaque |O |Elevated flat-topped area, usually more than 5 mm in | | | | |diameter | ANSWERS."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Pathology","displayTopic":"General and Systemic Pathology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["long_option_manual_review"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-b5a6da4e6a14","stem":"Which of the following is NOT associated with H.pylori infection?","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"General Pathology","topic":"General and Systemic Pathology","topicOriginal":"General and Systemic Pathology","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Adenocarcinoma of the gastro-esophageal junction."},{"label":"B","text":"Carcinoma of the stomach"},{"label":"C","text":"Duodenal ulcer"},{"label":"D","text":"Gastric ulcer"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":true,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"General Pathology","displayTop