ove condition (4 Marks) Predisposing factors of meningitis • Ear infections (Otitis media, mastoiditis) • Sinusitis • Respiratory infections • Malnutrition • Head injuries • Septicaemia and Diarrhea especially in the new-borns • Immune suppression e.g. HIV 23 SECTION E: GUIDED ESSAY QUESTIONS 30 MARKS INSTRUCTIONS • This section consists of two (2) questions which are supposed to be answered in a narrative way • Write your answer on a separate sheet of paper provided; each question should start on a new page. • Write your examination number on each answer sheet you are using. • Write a readable handwrite; DIRTY WORK IS NOT ALLOWED"}],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["topic_generic","mcq_missing_options"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Internal Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["long_option_manual_review","mcq_missing_options","not_enough_options","prior_structural_review_flag","repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":["option_whitespace_normalization"],"duplicateStemGroup":"ff401543f17f66de3a115f905240f87b4b79394c"},{"id":"q-ecb7fc5e73c6","stem":"What is the WHO clinical stage of the patient","type":"Clinical Vignette","subject":"Internal Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Internal Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-36d4b06077b5","stem":"Outline for (4) Possible causes of the above condition","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Internal Medicine","topic":"Unassigned top