 Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Internal Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Stimulation of glycogen synthesis in muscle fibre"},{"label":"B","text":"Inhibition of lipolysis in the adipocytes"},{"label":"C","text":"Stimulation of fatty acid hepatocytes synthesis in the"},{"label":"D","text":"Stimulation of fatty acid synthesis in muscle fibre"},{"label":"E","text":"Stimulation of gluconeogenesis in the hepatocyte"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Internal Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"74d99b341ff5b3f5bdfbec77db61dc5bc7793e43"},{"id":"q-118a552b512c","stem":"............................ Inhibit maturation of virus by interrupting the protein processing and virus assembly. Group B","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Microbiology","topic":"Virology","topicOriginal":"Virology","subtopic":"Viruses","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Pilocarpine"},{"label":"B","text":"Norepinephrine"},{"label":"C","text":"Lopinavir/Ritonavir"},{"label":"D","text":"Epinephrine"},{"label":"E","text":"Nevirapine"},{"label":"F","text":"Tetracycline"},{"label":"G","text":"Zidovudine"},{"label":"H","text":"ipratropium"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Microbiology","displayTopic":"Virology","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["too_many_options"],"cleaningOperations":["whitespace/page_marker_normalization"]},{"id":"q-ce88b3f2e408","stem":"Intravenous Verapamil","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Internal Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"May terminate supra ventricular tachycardia."},{"label":"B","text":"Must not be given to patients receiving beta blockers."},{"label":"C","text":"Reduces Digoxin excretion."},{"label":"D","text":"One must delay DC-cardio version at least 2 hours after a dose."},{"label":"E","text":"Shortens the PR-interval."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Internal Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"b2be618938eec53b9f8a5c63e9b90664c72f6ebc"},{"id":"q-8b749a720665","stem":"Nifedipine in comparison to Verapamil is more likely to","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Internal Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Worsen angina."},{"label":"B","text":"Cause ankle swelling unresponsive to diuretics."},{"label":"C","text":"Have a negative inotropic effects"},{"label":"D","text":"Cause flushing and headache."},{"label":"E","text":"Cause constipation."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Internal Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"19c09b47128faec7c8c69f64a9ccb1848b3b632d"},{"id":"q-3a82951b599a","stem":"The following statement about therapy with iron is true","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Internal Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Parenteral administration produces a more rapid rise in haemoglobin than oral administration.F"},{"label":"B","text":"Desferrioxamine is useful in the treatment over dosage with iron preparationT"},{"label":"C","text":"Ascorbic acid impairs the efficiency of iron absorption F"},{"label":"D","text":"Iron preparation should not be taken at same time as with tea which contains tannate.T"},{"label":"E","text":"Gastro-intestinal contains side effects which limit the use of oral iron preparations.T"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Internal Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"8f7e2ea421ed545e89fa47cd58a0da6f4a638d5d"},{"id":"q-db894b61a028","stem":"Folic acid","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Internal Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Alone provides adequate treatment for some cases of pernicious anemia F"},{"label":"B","text":"Is absorbed in the large intestine.F"},{"label":"C","text":"Is only active when converted to tetrahydrofolic acid. T"},{"label":"D","text":"Is not present in green vegetables other than spinachF"},{"label":"E","text":"Should be used routely in pregnancy in a dose of about 300ug a day.T"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["short_or_incomplete_stem","topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Internal Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","