xis of neutrophils (inhibit)"},{"label":"E","text":"increase the release of mast cell mediators (decrease)"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Internal Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"ddd203c01e9ef4e8892c4a524c358e744b3488a4"},{"id":"q-2031b5e4b481","stem":"Chloroquine, a 4-aminoquinoline used mainly to treat malaria.","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Internal Medicine","topic":"Infectious Diseases","topicOriginal":"Infectious Diseases","subtopic":"Malaria","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Has not been shown to have a role in the treatment of rheumatoid arthritis"},{"label":"B","text":"Does not inhibit phospholipase A2"},{"label":"C","text":"Does not reduce the formation of the eicosanoids"},{"label":"D","text":"May intercalate in the DNA and inhibit DNA and RNA synthesis, as it does in microorganisms"},{"label":"E","text":"Pharmacological effects in modifying rheumatoid disease appear in 4 days"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":[],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Internal Medicine","displayTopic":"Infectious Diseases","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":[],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-8d6a5151018b","stem":"Allopurinol is the drug of choice in the long-term treatment of gout","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Internal Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"It is highly effective in the treatment of an acute attack"},{"label":"B","text":"increases the effect of mercaptopurine, an antimetabolite that may be used in cancer chemotherapy"},{"label":"C","text":"it decreases the effect of azathioprine, which is metabolised to mercaptopurine"},{"label":"D","text":"It does not enhance the effect of an anticancer drug, cyclophosphamide"},{"label":"E","text":"Has important drug interaction with oral anticoagulants through enhancing their metabolism"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Internal Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"3063f692262e13f92ebe2b1590d6686956966f19"},{"id":"q-92fecebcb62c","stem":"Iron absorption","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Internal Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The site of absorption is duodenum and upper jejunum, and the process is passive"},{"label":"B","text":"The rapid uptake of iron across the brush border is rate limiting"},{"label":"C","text":"Transfer from the interior of the cell into the plasma is energy independent"},{"label":"D","text":"Haem iron is absorbed as intact haem and the iron is released in mucosal cell by the action of haem oxidase"},{"label":"E","text":"Is stored in the body as transferrin"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Internal Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"95c0bce0ad2d5b098ee8fd12dfb60c5da083c26c"},{"id":"q-b295fddd1526","stem":"The oral bioavailability of a drug, which of the following statements is not true","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Internal Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Is a measure of the extent to which it enters the systemic circulation"},{"label":"B","text":"May be influenced by changing excipient from calcium phosphate to lactose"},{"label":"C","text":"Is determined by comparing area under the plasma concentration time curve (AUC) following administration of two or more oral doses"},{"label":"D","text":"May be reduced by hepatic enzyme induction"},{"label":"E","text":"Two preparations of a drug may have similar bioavailability but have different peak concentrations."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Internal Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-10c82e6ca571","stem":"In repeated (multiple) dosing","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Internal Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"If the dosing interval is much greater than the T1/2, little if any drug accumulation occurs"},{"label":"B","text":"It takes approximately five T1/2 to reach 50% of steady state (Css) concentration"},{"label":"C","text":"If a drug is administered every the peak plasma concentration will be four times the trough concentration"},{"label":"D","text":"The use of a bolus loading dose increases the time taken to reach Css"},{"label":"E","text":"At Css concentration, the rate of drug absorption is lower than the rate of elimination"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Internal Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-ecf497bb7a24","stem":"Choose the most incorrect statement: Ethyl alcohol (ethanol)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Internal Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"The majority of oral ethanol is absorbed from the small intestine"},{"label":"B","text":"It delays gastric emptying"},{"label":"C","text":"95% of the ingested ethanol is metabolised"},{"label":"D","text":"Is second to heroin as the most important drug of dependence"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above are incorrect."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Internal Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-328f97a94a3f","stem":"Derilium tremens","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Internal Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Occurs in approximately 60% of patients withdrawing from alcohol"},{"label":"B","text":"Has a mortality of nearly 100%"},{"label":"C","text":"Benzodiazepines are contraindicated"},{"label":"D","text":"Thiamine should be administered parentetrally"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above are correct"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Internal Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-0ddaa5e6a5b9","stem":"Choose the most correct statement: The following drugs/poisons have been correctly paired with an appropriate antidote/specic measure","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Internal Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Paracetamol – acetylcysteine"},{"label":"B","text":"Iron – Desferrioxamine"},{"label":"C","text":"Dextropropxypehene – naoloxone"},{"label":"D","text":"Methanol – Ethanol"},{"label":"E","text":"All of the above SECTION II - TRUE/FALSE QUESTIONS An incomplete statement of phrases or questions is followed by five (5) completions or responses or answers. For each completion or response or answer write in the space provided TRUE for true and FALSE for false ones with respect to the incomplete statement or phrases or questions. ONE FULL MARK FOR EACH CORRECT ANSWER ZERO MARK FOR LEAVING BLANK PENALTY 0.1 MARKS FOR A WRONG GUESS"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Internal Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["answer_text_in_option","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-78ca15146db0","stem":"The non-steroid anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAIDs)","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Internal Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Are contraindicated in patients suffering from - Hypersensitive to salicylates or other NSAIDs - Asthmatic patient"},{"label":"B","text":"Must be avoided if possible in patients suffering from - Patient with renal failure - Patient with heart failure - Patient with Hypertension - Patient with edema"}],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["topic_generic","mcq_missing_options"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Internal Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["mcq_missing_options","not_enough_options","prior_structural_review_flag","repeated_question_stem","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"d813954a3040e50a51b91da959557e57e59f6c06"},{"id":"q-90147c4023bf","stem":"Mention 3 factors that determine the amount of drug bound to plasma proteins. (a) ______________________________________________________________ (b)______________________________________________________________ (c) ______________________________________________________________","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Internal Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Internal Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-83be1d304c72","stem":"With respect to the haemopoietic system","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Internal Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"What is the result of folic acid deficiency? - Congenital neural tube defect - Megaloblastic anemia"},{"label":"B","text":"Intrinsic factor is essential for Vitamin B12 absorption"}],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["topic_generic","mcq_missing_options"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswe