d of the presenting part."},{"label":"C","text":"Regular painful uterine contraction, dilatation of the cervix and descent of the presenting part."}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","displayTopic":"Labor and Delivery · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-d07507b9379d","stem":"The following are types of abruption placenta (3) Which statement on preeclampsia is correct? (4) Which statement on gestational diabetes is correct? (5) Which statement on anaemia in pregnancy is correct?","type":"OSCE / Practical Station","subject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","topic":"Antenatal Care · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Antenatal Care","options":[{"label":"D","text":"Concealed and revealed abruption placenta"},{"label":"E","text":"Revealed and overt placenta abruption"},{"label":"F","text":"Concealed and Vasa praevia"},{"label":"G","text":"None of the above (a) Preeclampsia only occurs in primigravidae."},{"label":"B","text":"Eclampsia is a serious complication of preeclampsia and has a high lethality."},{"label":"C","text":"Intravascular fluid overload is an important pathophysiological mechanism in the manifestation of preeclampsia."},{"label":"D","text":"All patients with preeclampsia show signs of renal failure."},{"label":"A","text":"Diabetes only occurs in elderly people but not in women in reproductive age. (b) All patients with gestational diabetes need insulin treatment."},{"label":"C","text":"Gestational diabetes only affects the pregnant woman but not the fetus."},{"label":"D","text":"Postpartum hypoglycaemia of the newborn is one of the complications of untreated gestational diabetes."},{"label":"A","text":"Severe anaemia in pregnancy is one of the major causes of maternal Mortality"}],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["topic_generic","too_many_options_possible_merge","duplicate_option_labels"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","displayTopic":"Antenatal Care · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_labels","prior_structural_review_flag","too_many_options_possible_merge","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-5612aab61ffa","stem":"(6) Which statement on malaria in pregnancy is correct?","type":"Short Answer","subject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","topic":"Antenatal Care · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Antenatal Care","options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","displayTopic":"Antenatal Care · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-e35b9a95e4b2","stem":"(7) Which of the following case histories suggests premature labour?","type":"Clinical Vignette","subject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","topic":"Labor and Delivery · Suggested","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":"Labor and Delivery","options":[],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Obstetrics and Gynecology","displayTopic":"Labor and Delivery · Suggested","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-8353a3951440","stem":"Which of the following combinations of parity, stage of delivery and duration 