t":"Posterior at 3 months, anterior at 18 months"},{"label":"C","text":"Posterior at 1 month, anterior at 6-8 months"},{"label":"D","text":"Posterior at 9 months, anterior at 9-12 months 6 Which of the following are signs of severe dehydration"},{"label":"A","text":"irritability, drinking eagerly"},{"label":"B","text":"very sunken eyes"},{"label":"C","text":"reduced skin turgor"},{"label":"D","text":"lethargy 7 Infant born to HIV-infected mothers should be started on PCP (Pneumonistic Carinii Pneumonia) prophylaxis at the following age."},{"label":"A","text":"at birth"},{"label":"B","text":"(b)2 weeks old"},{"label":"C","text":"© 4-6 weeks old"},{"label":"D","text":"(d) 2 months of age 8 The normal range for a newborn heart rate is :"},{"label":"A","text":"60-80"},{"label":"B","text":"80-100"},{"label":"C","text":"110-150"},{"label":"D","text":"140-200"}],"priority":0,"status":"review","flags":["topic_generic","too_many_options_possible_merge","duplicate_option_labels"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"review_required","auditFlags":["duplicate_option_labels","nonunique_option_labels","prior_structural_review_flag","repeated_question_stem","too_many_options","too_many_options_possible_merge","topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[],"duplicateStemGroup":"84637561f1b062ae6b1c06e8d694e92929c255c2"},{"id":"q-a55efb539f34","stem":"An infant born at 32 weeks of gestation and weighing 1000g should be classified as","type":"OSCE / Practical Station","subject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Low birth weight and small for gestational age"},{"label":"B","text":"premature"},{"label":"C","text":"Small for gestational age"},{"label":"D","text":"premature and small for