- bilateral increased patellar and biceps tendon reflexes - bilateral sustained ankle clonus This condition is best described as","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Internal Medicine","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"Spastic hemiplegia"},{"label":"B","text":"Decerebrate position"},{"label":"C","text":"Spastic quadriplegia"},{"label":"D","text":"Dyskinetic cerebral plasy"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Internal Medicine","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-2eaebded5b2d","stem":"A child of 3 months should have all of the following abilities EXCEPT","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","topic":"Unassigned topic","topicOriginal":"General","subtopic":"","suggestedTopic":null,"options":[{"label":"A","text":"should be able to smile"},{"label":"B","text":"should be able to reach out and grasp for objects"},{"label":"C","text":"should be able to follow objects through a complete arc"},{"label":"D","text":"should be able to hold the neck upright for a short time"}],"priority":0,"status":"practice_draft","flags":["topic_generic"],"keyVerified":false,"hasSourceAnswer":false,"needsFigure":false,"displaySubject":"Pediatrics and Child Health","displayTopic":"Unassigned topic","answerAuditStatus":"not_adjudicated","sourceAnswerTrusted":false,"publicationStatus":"unverified_draft","auditFlags":["topic_generic"],"cleaningOperations":[]},{"id":"q-09fe958aa47f","stem":"An upper motor neuron facial nerve palsy caused by a brain infarct in the left hemisphere ( internal capsule) will present with the following findings","type":"Single Best Answer MCQ","subject":"Internal Medicin